### Lab 02: SQLite Database and CRUD Routes
### Tested via VS Code REST Client

### 1. GET All Books
GET http://localhost:3000/books/
Accept: application/json

### 2. GET Book by ID (Existing: ID 1)
GET http://localhost:3000/books/1/
Accept: application/json

### 3. GET Book by ID (Non-existent: ID 999 - Expect 404)
GET http://localhost:3000/books/999/
Accept: application/json

### 4. POST Add a New Book
POST http://localhost:3000/books/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Design Patterns: Elements of Reusable Object-Oriented Software",
  "author": "Erich Gamma, Richard Helm, Ralph Johnson, John Vlissides",
  "price": 750,
  "pages": 395
}

### 5. PUT Update an Existing Book (Update ID 1)
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/1/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone (Special Illustrated Edition)",
  "author": "J.K. Rowling",
  "price": 520,
  "pages": 350
}

### 6. DELETE a Book by ID (Delete ID 5)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/books/5/
Accept: application/json
